okay we're gonna get back into some more  Doctor Who stuff I've already done a  little bit of ranking I rank the doctors  I'm now gonna do a ranking of companions  and a couple of things before I get  started firstly I'm only going to deal  with companions from the modern era of  Doctor Who starting with Christopher  Eccleston going forward if I were to do  classic companions this thing would be  an hour and a half long secondly I need  to clarify how I am choosing to define a  companion I have two requirements  firstly they have to appear in more than  one story and to be clear two parters  count as a single story that's the first  thing so that gets rid of any one-off  characters secondly we need to have seen  them be in the TARDIS for a trip with  those requirements that gives me 15 that  we got to be tackling here let's get  right into it starting with the bottom  of the barrel Angie and already I'm not  gonna spend a lot of time on these two  because I really wish I didn't even have  to deal with them but unfortunately they  meet the requirement they were just  horrible all they do is complain  secondly they do absolutely nothing to  move the plot forward you could  literally remove them from the plot  completely and almost nothing about the  story changes they are completely  useless moving on number fourteen Adam  Mitchell this guy's also completely  useless the difference though is he at  least was supposed to be completely  useless Adam Mitchell is a bad companion  by design he was written to be that way  so that it shows that rose Tyler's  ability to cope with everything that was  going on with being with the doctor was  not a universal gift a lot of people  can't cope going up slightly we get to  Jackie Tyler  now Jackie Kai was another one I kind of  wish I didn't have to deal with she  exemplifies the the whole domestic thing  there's almost been nothing brought to  the table with all the domestics all but  the family the brothers siblings parents  especially once or twice it was kind of  interesting because it was a side we  hadn't really seen before in the classic  series but it got old real quick and I  wish they would all just go away next on  the agenda Clara Oswald  I loved her chemistry with Matt Smith  but in truth she's a much better plot  point than she is a character she's very  very thinly drawn  I actually prefer her appearances in  asylum of the Daleks and the snowman I  feel like there was actually more depth  in those earlier incarnations than in  the woman the version of Clara that we  actually got to spend a lot more time  with she's getting a little bit better  now that the whole mystery of the  impossible girl has been addressed but  it still just she feels very flimsy to  me and that brings us to Brian Williams  Rory's father again he gets on the lower  end for being part of the whole domestic  thing he ranks higher than Jackie Tyler  though because he is inherently likable  Jackie Tyler is inherently grading he's  just a sweet guy and you get where a lot  of the things that are wonderful about  Rory come from so it's kind of a nice  insight but ultimately I can take them  or leave them that brings us to number  10 the last of the double digits and I  got to be really careful on how I  explain this one because I'm going to  get a lot of heat for it Sarah Jane  Smith I made the decision to only take  into consideration modern-era main show  appearances I am NOT considering any of  her work in the classic era nor am i  considering it anything that she  appeared in in spin-offs she's a piece  of nostalgia brilliantly executed  nostalgia don't do not get me wrong but  her peak as a companion was in the  classic era especially when she was  paired with Tom Baker now I mean she's  nice it's nice to have her there but she  doesn't bring as much to the proceedings  beyond just a sort of oh cool check it  out thing that oh I feel the ones I've  ranked above her they just bring more to  the table in their appearances in the  modern era number 9 Martha Jones  she's the rebound companion we know it  the doctor knows it ultimately Martha  knows it I can certainly appreciate and  respect her as a character but in the  scope of the doctor she's always gonna  be middling to lower-ranking just  because of where she came in in his time  stream  yeah that's just gonna be the way it is  number 8 Mickey Smith  and Mickey was interesting because the  journey he went through Mickey when he  started out was kind of annoying he was  almost as bad as Jackie and his early  appearances but he went through a  transformation and a journey through his  experiences that by the end not only is  are you happy to see him when he turns  up but he's turned into a badass and  it's all very believable we get it in  these little measured doses and you can  see the change happening I think we got  just enough Mickey Smith to make that  transformation believable too much more  of him would have gotten old I think he  was very well balanced number 7 Rose  Tyler  I do like Rose Tyler I was never as  enamored with her as some people wore  just because she did well she did some  stupid stuff for no reason other than to  kind of show how the doctor deals with  people when they do stupid things  she still wonderfully charming she's a  lot of fun definitely Billie Piper  really brought that to the rule and that  is really what carries her through on  paper she wavers a little bit you put  her in Billy Piper's hands and she  brings a charm to the whole thing that  actually makes it work number six Jack  Harkness now again remember I'm not  taking spin-off material into  consideration here which unlike Sarah  Jane Smith is actually in Jack Harkness  is favored because I don't particularly  like what they do with him and Torchwood  they make him into this very tortured  hour figure where what's great about him  in the main series is how fun he is he's  he's definitely at his best when he's  playing alongside Christopher Eccleston  because he brings something to the  proceedings that Christopher Eccleston  just doesn't have the more dashing  heroic hey kind of character now he  doesn't work quite as well when he's  with David Tennant cuz David Tennant has  that same thing going on so he Jack  becomes a little bit redundant but he's  still fun to have around and every time  he turns up it makes me smile  number five Rory Williams here was  another one that a bit like Mickey we  get the boyfriend who is annoying at  first but then he goes through a whole  journey and a transformation and with  Rory oh my god by the end I just I loved  him you get to know his relationship  with Amy he's kind of her punching bag a  little bit you think oh that's sweet but  sad  but then once amy comes to appreciate  him and you see the lengths that he goes  through to be with her it's wonderful  and the two of them together are just  dynamite and even rory when interacting  directly with the doctor is great when  he punches the doctor or when he  confronts the Cybermen where is my wife  oh it's it's fantastic stuff and when  he's put into conflict because of Amy  you get the best out of it number four  the always controversial river song I  love the very concept of her that she  meets the doctor completely out of order  but we never feel like we know her  enough that we can completely trust her  you always feel like she's pulling one  over on the doctor and pulling one over  on us as an audience and I kind of like  that feeling personally I guess it bugs  some people but I think she's a lot of  fun and I regret that we have probably  seen the end of her at this point pretty  much everything about her has gotten  tied up by now with the exception of  exactly how she learned the doctor's  name which still bugs me that that  hasn't been addressed but I may just  have to deal with it number three  Amy Pond now I love the way the doctor  meets Amy Pond I love the way that their  relationship develops because the fact  that she was enamored with him as a  child  but also that he abandoned her really  informs their relationship because she  is astounded by him and in awe of him  but at the same time kind of fed up with  him and she doesn't take any of his crap  I love their dynamic and she's even  better when paired with Rory the three  of them together the doctor Rory Amy I  just love that trio number two Wilfred  mops I love this guy and I really really  wish he could have been a longer term  companion Bernard Cribbins has this  feistiness to him that's just perfect to  pair him with someone who is physically  young but much much older the two of  them together the dynamic is so  wonderful it's so good and he breaks my  heart when he tries to give the doctor  the gun on the ship of the doctor one  take it he is so good and he's wonderful  and he's funny and he's sad and he's  almost everything I wanted my companion  not quite though because he didn't get  the top spot top spot goes to Donna  Noble she is the best friend the  romantic angle has been overplayed  severely just so sick of it Donna never  a question there was never even a hint  or an inkling in fact her outright  disgust at the very suggestion of  romantic involvement of the doctor  coupled with a wonderful chemistry and  the fact that like Amy she's able to  call him out on stuff and then just her  energy fact that she's a little bit  older that makes a lot of difference  everything that Catherine Tate is able  to bring to this role and when she's  working with David Tennant it's just  they bounce off each other in the best  possible way because she thinks about  things in a different way from the  doctor she has a much more blunt  approach to thing and that contrasts  with his more nuanced and finesse way of  going at things and thinking about him  and it's great just to see him bounce  off each other and then for them to come  together and work together it's always  fantastic stuff at every moment and then  what happens to her it hurts and it's  painful in the most beautiful way that  those sorts of things can be painful and  she takes the number one spot so there  we have it the companions of the doctor  ranks from the bottom of the barrel why  did they even show up to the very top  why can't they just travel in the TARDIS  forever I like to think that I justified  my ranking but you know what if you got  a different favorite than mine good for  you you should everybody's got their  favorites that's the beauty of Doctor  Who it's always changing it's always  renewing this why we love it and that's  why I cannot wait till we get more I  need to see Peter Capaldi and what he's  gonna do it's gonna be a long wait it'll  be worth it and until then this  council's adjourned
 

